Test is INVALID on x86-64: gcc and clang both reject "ap = 0" (va_list is __va_list_tag[1]; assignment to array type) — the "ok" expect encodes a scalar-va_list model. madc currently accepts the __builtin_va_list assignment (line 9, divergent) and rejects the va_list one (line 10, gcc-parity). Rework filed: map __builtin_va_list to the target's real va_list type, then convert this to an .expect_err gcc-parity test and lift. Audit 2026-07-19.
